# =============================================================================
#  ISPFlow — FreeRADIUS dictionary.
#
#  Two groups of attributes:
#
#    1. NETISP:: control attributes. These carry values between the SQL queries
#       and the unlang policy inside a single request. They are internal and are
#       never placed in a reply, so they are declared as internal rather than
#       with vendor numbers that would collide on the wire.
#
#    2. Mikrotik vendor attributes. These DO go on the wire. Defining them
#       explicitly is what stops FreeRADIUS from silently dropping a value it has
#       no dictionary entry for — the usual reason "Mikrotik-Rate-Limit works in
#       the lab but not in production".
#
#  This file must be referenced from /etc/freeradius/3.0/dictionary with
#  $INCLUDE dictionary.netisp. On a stock install it is present on disk but NOT
#  referenced, so every Mikrotik-* attribute is treated as unknown and silently
#  dropped. install-vps.sh adds the reference.
# =============================================================================

# A VENDOR line needs BOTH a name and an enterprise number, and FreeRADIUS
# rejects `VENDOR Netisp` on its own as `invalid VENDOR entry`.
#
# 64500 is inside the IANA range reserved for documentation and examples
# (64496-64511), so it cannot collide with a real vendor.
#
# The name must also match the attribute prefix, because unlang references these
# as `NETISP::LookupKey`. FreeRADIUS resolves `::` against the vendor that owns
# the attribute, so the vendor is `Netisp` and the attributes are `NETISP-*`.
VENDOR        Netisp               64500

BEGIN-VENDOR    Netisp

# Values returned by queries.conf and consumed by the inline policy.
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-LookupKey        1  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-AccountStatus    2  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-ExpiresAt        3  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-RateLimit        4  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-SimultaneousUse  5  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-ClientId         6  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-PlanName         7  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-IspId            8  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-SessionStart     9  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-SessionRowId    10  string
ATTRIBUTE   NETISP-AcctUpdated     11  string

END-VENDOR      Netisp

# ── Mikrotik attributes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NOT redefined here. FreeRADIUS ships dictionary.mikrotik with
# Mikrotik-Rate-Limit, Mikrotik-Expires, Mikrotik-Simultaneous-Limit,
# Mikrotik-Group and Mikrotik-Wireless-Forward already defined. Redeclaring them
# aborts startup with
#   dict_addattr: Duplicate attribute name Mikrotik-Rate-Limit
#
# The shipped dictionary is pulled in by install-vps.sh with
#   $INCLUDE dictionary.mikrotik
# from /etc/freeradius/3.0/dictionary, which on a stock install it is not: the
# file exists on disk but nothing references it, so every Mikrotik-* attribute is
# treated as unknown and silently dropped from the Access-Accept. That is the
# usual reason "Mikrotik-Rate-Limit works in the lab but not in production".
